To be considered valid and reportable, a notification must contain the greatest amount of information possible, including at least the following data:

*   Identification of the notifier [RDC 406/2020, Art. 32, I];
*   Identification of the patient (name or initials; or gender; or age or date of birth) [RDC 406/2020, Art. 32, II];
*   Description of the Adverse Event [RDC 406/2020, Art. 32, III]; and
*   Name of the suspect medication [RDC 406/2020, Art. 32, IV].

If any of this information is missing, the initial report is considered incomplete, and the Marketing Authorization Holder is obligated to actively seek the missing data [RDC 406/2020, Art. 32, Parágrafo único].

