Under RDC 751/2022, when providing instructions for use in a non-printed format, the following information must be included on the external label or in a document attached to the product if the label dimensions do not allow for it:

*   The method to obtain the correlation between the supplied product and the corresponding version of the instructions for use [RDC 751/2022, Art. 51, I and § 1º];
*   Indication of a Consumer Service (SAC) where the printed format of the instructions for use can be requested at no additional cost, including shipping [RDC 751/2022, Art. 51, II and § 1º];
*   A guarantee that the instructions for use will be available throughout the entire period the product is on the market, which is considered the product's useful life starting from the last unit sold [RDC 751/2022, Art. 51, III and § 2º]; and
*   Specification of the resources required for the user to read the instructions for use [RDC 751/2022, Art. 51, IV and § 1º].

